      <h2>Dive the Pacific Northwest the way it should be done</h2>
      <p class="lead">The water is cold. The diving is packed with life.</p>
      <p>The San Juan Islands sit in the middle of the Salish Sea, where strong tidal currents feed walls and reefs covered in anemones, sponges and fish. It's some of the richest cold water diving anywhere.</p>
      <p>On a Supernova expedition the yacht is your basecamp. Our 21 foot aluminum landing craft runs as a live boat, with a front loading bow gate for easy water entry, so we can reach remote dive sites few divers ever see.</p>
      <p>Between dives, refill tanks on the onboard compressor, take a hot shower in your stateroom and sit down to fresh Northwest food.</p>

      <h2>What a dive day looks like</h2>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>Breakfast aboard while we move to the day's first site</li>
        <li>Load up the landing craft and run in close to the dive spot</li>
        <li>Live boat pickup after each dive, no swimming back to an anchor line</li>
        <li>Tank fills on Supernova's compressor between dives</li>
        <li>Paddle, kayak or hike the islands when you're off gassing</li>
        <li>Hot shower, dinner at anchor, repeat</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who this trip is for</h2>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>Certified divers who want more than a day boat can offer</li>
        <li>Free divers looking for clear, life filled cold water</li>
        <li>Dive buddies and couples who want a private stateroom</li>
        <li>Small dive clubs who want to charter the whole boat</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Diving questions</h2>
